# Naming Convention Specification
This document defines the mandatory naming conventions for all media assets
used in the Football Coaching App. These conventions ensure consistency,
automation compatibility, and predictable Supabase storage paths.

---

## 1. GENERAL RULES (APPLY TO ALL FILES)

- All filenames must be **lowercase**
- Use **hyphens** instead of spaces or underscores
- All session numbers must be **zero‑padded** (001, 002, 003…)
- Filenames must remain **stable** once uploaded (no renaming)
- File extensions must be **lowercase**

---

## 2. PITCH DIAGRAMS (PNG)

Used for pitch layout images displayed in the app.

Format:
pitch-u9-session-001.png  
pitch-u9-session-002.png  
pitch-u9-session-003.png  

Rules:
- PNG format only
- Stored in `/media/pitch-diagrams/u9/`
- One diagram per session
- Aspect ratio defined in the Media Format Standard

---

## 3. VIDEO THUMBNAILS (PNG)

Used for fast-loading preview images for demo videos.

Format:
thumb-u9-session-001.png  

Rules:
- PNG format
- 16:9 aspect ratio
- Stored in `/media/video-thumbnails/u9/`

---

## 4. VIDEOS (MP4)

Only applies if videos are self-hosted in Supabase.

Format:
video-u9-session-001.mp4  

Rules:
- MP4 format
- Stored in `/media/videos/u9/`
- If using YouTube/Vimeo, store only the URL in the database

---

## 5. LESSON FILES (OPTIONAL)

If lesson files are exported or stored locally:

Format:
lesson-u9-001.md  
lesson-u9-002.md  

Rules:
- Lowercase
- Hyphens
- Zero-padded lesson numbers

---

## 6. FUTURE AGE GROUPS

Naming conventions must scale consistently:

Examples:
pitch-u10-session-001.png  
thumb-u11-session-004.png  
video-u12-session-010.mp4  

---

## 7. RATIONALE

These naming conventions ensure:
- Predictable Supabase paths
- Easy automation and batch processing
- Clean, scalable asset libraries
- No broken URLs in the app
- Consistency across all age groups and future expansions

